## 1. Analysis & Pre-Thinking

**Core requirements (from your report + the mockup):**
1. The **activity filter chips are invisible** — a sticky-offset bug, not a data bug.
2. The **post author avatar fails** — a broken fallback renderer + fragile account resolution.
3. The overall wall is a poor re-implementation of the mockup — layout/quality issues.

**Root causes I confirmed in the code:**

| Problem | Root cause |
|---|---|
| **Filter bar hidden** | In `Wall.vue`, the header (title+tabs) is `sticky top-0 z-20` and the kind-filter bar is a *separate* `sticky top-0 z-10`. Both stick to the same `top-0`, so the filters slide **underneath** the header and disappear. |
| **Avatar fails** | `WallAvatar.vue` renders the fallback as `<span :class="avatarClass(seed)">{{label}}</span>` — the span has a background colour but **no width/height/flex**, so it collapses into floating text with no circle. Also `wallEvents.js` indexes accounts only by a single id, so a post whose `authorId` is a *username* doesn't resolve and falls back to the bot. |
| **Bad mockup fidelity** | The 3-column grid isn't centered on wide screens (`max-w` wrapper missing); the post card/action bar are rough; the composer is missing the toolbar and always-visible counter. |

**Store facts verified:** `$storex.meets.allActiveMeets`, `$storex.kanban.allBoards`, `$storex.kanban.boardChats(id)`, `$storex.chats.loadChats()`, `$storex.api.userNetwork`, `$storex.users.user` all exist — so the data plumbing is valid; only the **presentation + resolution** were broken.

**Target files (all inside `src/components/wall/`):**
- `Wall.vue` — fix sticky header/filters, center the grid, tighten layout.
- `WallAvatar.vue` — proper circular fallback + image error handling.
- `wallEvents.js` — multi-key account indexing + logo bot avatar + safe palette.
- `WallPostCard.vue` — mockup-faithful card + action bar.
- `WallComposer.vue` — toolbar + always-visible counter.
- `WallTimeline.vue` — robust author resolution fallback.

